<article class="env-lemma" id="0GRD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GRD">Lemma <span data-tag="0GRD">103.17.9</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a locally Noetherian algebraic stack. Let $\mathcal{F}$ and $\mathcal{G}$ be coherent be $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X}$-modules. Then the internal hom $hom(\mathcal{F}, \mathcal{G})$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0GQN" data-tag="0GQN">103.10.8</a> is a coherent $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X}$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U \to \mathcal{X}$ be a smooth surjective morphism from a scheme. By item (<a href="/tag/0GQT" data-tag="0GQT">12</a>) in Section <a href="/tag/0GQS" data-tag="0GQS">103.12</a> we see that the restriction of $hom(\mathcal{F}, \mathcal{G})$ to $U$ is the Hom sheaf of the restrictions. Hence this lemma follows from the case of algebraic spaces, see Cohomology of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/07UE" data-tag="07UE">69.12.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>